      "side": 1,
      "message": "Naming is a little confused in Soong.  Name() was supposed to be used only once, when Blueprint was reading the Android.bp files to provide an original name for the module, overridden by some modules like prebuilts in order to provdie a \"prebuilt_\" prefix.  Then later uses are expected to use ModuleContext.ModuleName(), ModuleContext.OtherModuleName(module), or Singleton.ModuleName(module), which will return the name taking into account things like TopDownMutatorContext.Rename.  Unfortunately Module.Name() is temptingly named and hard to avoid usages.  BaseModuleName() is basically Name() without the prefix.  The usage below is fine, but maybe we should replace it with something on the prebuilt interface that returns the name without the prefix.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
